Fix a real upstream build bug (not an AXOS feature): release/src/router/rc/services.c's
apply_config_to_driver() / apply_config_to_driver_wlc() are unconditional core
WLAN-config-apply functions (not gated by RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD) that live
inside the prebuilt rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/broadcom.o — which rc/Makefile
links in unconditionally (see rc/Makefile's `broadcom.o:` prebuild-override
rule, itself unconditional). Confirmed via `nm` on that prebuilt object:
apply_config_to_driver() needs (references as undefined) two symbols,
wpa_supp_get_config_filename and wpa_supp_create_config_file. Those two are
only DEFINED in rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/hostapd_config_6e.o (also confirmed via
`nm` — every other GT-AX6000 prebuilt object was checked and none of them
provide these). But rc/Makefile only adds hostapd_config_6e.o (or
hostapd_config.o) to `rc`'s OBJS when RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD is "y" — so once
RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD is genuinely off (see firmware/build.sh and
0003-gt-ax6000-sys-util-gen-util-hostapd-decoupling.patch), the object that
provides these two unconditionally-needed helper functions never gets built
in, while the unconditional code that needs them still does.

Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` (RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD
genuinely off) fails linking `rc` with "undefined reference to
`wpa_supp_get_config_filename'" and "...to `wpa_supp_create_config_file'".

Fix: drop the RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD requirement from just this one OBJS
addition (hostapd_config_6e.o / hostapd_config.o), leaving the rest of that
Makefile block (the wpa_supplicant/WPS_PBCD-daemon-specific CFLAGS, LDFLAGS,
and OBJS_WPS_PBCD additions) still correctly gated on RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD,
since those really are hostapd-specific. This is a general Makefile
inconsistency — the same shape as 0003's sys_util/gen_util fix — not
something specific to disabling hostapd for this model.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0003. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.
diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/Makefile b/release/src/router/rc/Makefile
index f52a36d5f4..a0ba6019a9 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/Makefile
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/Makefile
@@ -903,7 +903,12 @@ LDFLAGS += -L$(TOP)/libasuslog -lasuslog
 CFLAGS += -I$(TOP)/libasuslog
 endif
 
-ifeq ($(RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD),y)
+# services.c's apply_config_to_driver()/apply_config_to_driver_wlc() are
+# unconditional (not gated by RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD) and, via the
+# unconditionally-linked prebuild/broadcom.o, need wpa_supp_get_config_filename
+# and wpa_supp_create_config_file — provided only by hostapd_config_6e.o /
+# hostapd_config.o. So this OBJS addition must NOT be gated on
+# RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD either, even though the rest of this hostapd block is.
 ifeq ($(or $(RTCONFIG_WIFI6E),$(HND_ROUTER_AX_6756),$(RTCONFIG_BCM_502L07P2)),y)
 OBJS += $(if $(wildcard sysdeps/broadcom/hostapd_config_6e.c),hostapd_config_6e.o,prebuild/hostapd_config_6e.o)
 else
@@ -911,8 +916,6 @@ OBJS += $(if $(wildcard sysdeps/broadcom/hostapd_config.c),hostapd_config.o,preb
 endif
 vpath %.c sysdeps/broadcom
 
-endif
-
 CFLAGS += -I$(TOP)/wlceventd
 LDFLAGS2 = $(LDFLAGS)
 
